- **Native AR3012 bootstrap re-enumeration recovery (2026-11-10):**
  `SimpleATHUsbBluetooth::start` now treats a successful switch-identity
  request and an ambiguous partial firmware upload as actual USB recovery
  work, rather than publishing only a `UsbResetRequired` property. After
  closing the firmware interface it schedules the pinned MacKernelSDK
  `IOUSBHostDevice::reset` on a separate kernel thread-call worker (the USB
  port workloop is forbidden for this API). A retained device/service pair
  stays alive until the callback exits. Before reset, the worker checks the
  old device remains active with the exact original USB vendor, product and
  revision, so it never deliberately resets an already-reenumerated HCI
  controller. Revoked USB epochs or downloads without writes are not reset.
  The portable `shouldReenumerateAth3k` decision has a seven-case synthetic
